      "scr_dup": "001",
      "evalb_id": "K2",
      "score_rate": 15,
      "evalb_memo": "Groups of 3 to 4 students will give a 25-to-30-minute oral presentation on the texts we read in this course. Each week, one group will present during the first hour of the class (after the quiz, if there is one), from March 19th to June 18th, with a total of 12 groups presenting through the semester. All oral presentations should include three parts: (1) an introduction to the assigned texts; (2) a close reading of a selected character and/or passage of interest; and (3) a Q & A section where the presenters and the audience can engage in discussions on the presentation and other related questions. Students have complete freedom in how they organize and deliver their presentations, but the bottom line is that everyone in the group must participate and present.",
      "evalb_memo_en": null,
      "evalb_name": "口頭報告",
      "evalb_name_en": "Oral presentation",
      "seq": 2
